  "facts": [
    "Native materializes canonical base64 data URI to inline bytes and detects MIME;20MiB cap and optional image normalization. file URI rereads original paths, so app must not pass renderer URI.",
    "Native session.prompt resume:false admits item but omits execution.wake; only a future fresh no-active synthetic compatibility probe may use it, never public production send.",
    "Native fork before validates actual parent message ID and emits before boundary; default fork is throughlatest and is not edit/retry semantics.",
    "Native media path supports PNG/JPEG/GIF/WebP/PDF; BMP/AVIF detection does not imply attachmentContent support. Unsupported model media is replaced with text downstream, so app must preblock explicit unsupported inputs.",
    "Current app send is text-only and idle-only; original digest/policy/retained authority remains binding."
  ]
